export const fieldNotes=`The Echo Chamber\nA first-person puzzle inspired by COMPSS 211A: Computing I.\n\nThe doorway responded to the sources represented in the beam, rather than its brightness. Two lamps could carry the very same source. Removing a repeated contribution reduced the glow but improved the signal. Removing the only contribution from another source left a gap.\n\nThe lesson is a research habit: trace where observations come from before treating them as independent evidence. A larger-looking result can contain repeated information.\n\nThe physical cables, shared markings, pulse rhythms, and receiver behavior all describe the same underlying circuit. The wiring changes when you start again. You can make mistakes, undo them, and find several valid solutions.\n\nCourse: https://github.com/macss-berkeley/compss-211a\n`;
